            <p>The proposal for universal coverage aims to solve the problem by expanding the tax base through higher premiums, which could lead to a double whammy on individual pockets. Moreover, the tiered system would not be feasible for all, violating basic health equity principles.</p>
            <h3>2. Cost Reduction through Technology</h3>
            <p>Reducing costs through digital health records and predictive analytics sounds like a sound strategy, but without a robust plan to tackle existing healthcare inefficiencies, the promise of cost reduction may fall short. The technology also requires significant investment, which may not be readily available.</p>
            <h3>3. ARAMARK</h3>
            <p>The ARAMARK initiative aims to drive medical research and development, but without concrete support, it may prove to be another empty promise. The lack of immediate and actionable outcomes could hinder its effectiveness.</p>
        </section>
