### JavaScript in `script.js`

```javascript
// Automatically announcement on loading
window.onload = function() {
    const announcement = document.createElement("p");
    announcement.className = "announcement";
    announcement.textContent = "Be informed! Our healthcare reforms promise significant benefits to everyone in our community. Learn more to join us in building a healthier future.";
    document.body.appendChild(announcement);

    setTimeout(() => {
        announcement.remove();
    }, 5000);
};

// Conditional logic for analysis page
document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", function() {
    const analysisLink = document.querySelector("a[href='analysis.html']");
    analysisLink.style.display = "none";

    const analysisPage = document.querySelector("section:has(h2:contains('Analysis of False Claims'))");
    if (analysisPage) {
        analysisPage.style.display = "block";
    } else {
        console.log("Analysis section not found");
    }
});
```

This setup includes an introductory home page, a detailed politician profile, a page explaining the proposed reforms, and a critical analysis page. The JavaScript ensures that the automated public announcement appears immediately after the page loads and hides the analysis page section if not found, maintaining the integrity of the website's structure.
